736	    /**
737	     * Flags a newly created owner as a possible (soft) duplicate. Reaching this point means the
738	     * owner already cleared {@link #rejectDuplicateIdentity(OwnerFieldsDto)}, so it does not share
739	     * an existing owner's identity key. A member that declared its household via
740	     * {@code sharesHousehold} is a deliberate addition to a known household, not a suspected
741	     * duplicate, so it is never flagged. Otherwise it is a possible duplicate when an existing owner
742	     * shares the Soundex code of its {@code lastName} and its {@code postcode} while carrying a
743	     * different identity key (see {@link #findPossibleDuplicate(Owner)}). When such an owner is
744	     * found, {@code possibleDuplicate} is set {@code true} and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} to the
745	     * matching owner's id; otherwise {@code possibleDuplicate} is set {@code false} and no matching
746	     * id is recorded. An owner without a postcode can share no postcode and is never a possible
747	     * duplicate.
748	     *
749	     * @param owner the owner being created, already carrying its normalized telephone and postcode
750	     * @param ownerFieldsDto the submitted owner fields carrying the {@code sharesHousehold} flag
751	     */
752	    private void applyPossibleDuplicate(Owner owner, OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
753	        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(false);
754	        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(null);
755	        if (sharesHousehold(ownerFieldsDto)) {
756	            return;
757	        }
758	        findPossibleDuplicate(owner).ifPresent(existing -> {
759	            owner.setPossibleDuplicate(true);
760	            owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(existing.getId());
761	        });
762	    }
763	
764	    /**
765	     * Finds the existing owner, if any, that makes the given newly created owner a possible (soft)
766	     * duplicate: a non-deleted owner whose {@code lastName} shares the new owner's Soundex code (see
767	     * {@link Owner#soundex(String)}) and whose {@code postcode} matches, while carrying a different
768	     * identity key (see {@link Owner#identityKey(String, String, String)}). Requiring a differing
769	     * identity key keeps a hard duplicate — already rejected with 409 by
770	     * {@link #rejectDuplicateIdentity(OwnerFieldsDto)} — from also being flagged as a soft match, so
771	     * the two household members whose telephones differ (hence differing identity keys, but matching
772	     * Soundex and postcode) are exactly the soft matches surfaced here. This is the single definition
773	     * of the soft-duplicate match; {@link #applyPossibleDuplicate(Owner, OwnerFieldsDto)} only records
774	     * the outcome on the owner. An owner without a postcode can share no postcode and matches nothing,
775	     * so {@link java.util.Optional#empty()} is returned.
776	     *
777	     * @param owner the owner being created, already carrying its normalized telephone and postcode
778	     * @return the matching existing owner, or {@link java.util.Optional#empty()} when none matches
779	     */
780	    private java.util.Optional<Owner> findPossibleDuplicate(Owner owner) {
781	        if (owner.getPostcode() == null) {
782	            return java.util.Optional.empty();
783	        }
784	        String soundex = Owner.soundex(owner.getLastName());
785	        String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
786	        return this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
787	            .filter(existing -> !Owner.isDeleted(existing.getDeleted()))
788	            .filter(existing -> !identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey())
789	                && soundex.equals(Owner.soundex(existing.getLastName()))
790	                && owner.getPostcode().equals(existing.getPostcode()))
791	            .findFirst();
792	    }
